  "description": "The language algorithms shared by the Broiler JavaScript engines: number conversion (Number::toString at every radix, toFixed, toExponential, toPrecision, StringToNumber, parseInt, parseFloat, numeric literal values, numeric keys and the string white-space set), numerics (the integer conversions, Float16, the Math kernels, exact rounding and the BigInt kernel) and text (UTF-16, padding and relative indices, replacement templates, the URI, base64 and hex codecs, and JSON's grammar, quoting and gap) and Date (the time-value arithmetic, the ISO calendar's civil-day helpers, the local-time provider with LocalTime and UTC, Date.parse's grammar in a strict and a Broiler.VM dialect, and the Date renderings) and time zones and calendar years (the decoder of the time-zone and calendar tables an engine hands in, lookup and primary identifiers, offsets and transitions with no 2037 cliff, possible instants, disambiguation, the start of a day, the offset time zones, and the Chinese, Korean, Umm al-Qura and Persian years) and the Temporal core's records and limits, balancing, regulation and addition, ISO 8601 / RFC 9557 grammar and string forms, and its calendars (the calendar identifiers of the Intl era and month code proposal, the Gregorian family, Coptic, Ethiopian, Indian, tabular Hijri and Hebrew calendars, the Chinese, Korean, Umm al-Qura and Persian calendars over their years, month codes, eras, month-day reference years, and calendar addition and difference) and its durations, rounding and differences (sign, balance and addition of durations, compare, round and total with and without relativeTo through calendar and time-zone providers, and until and since of every type), with the WorkCharge metering delegate, the ResultStatus enumeration and the limit records every shared operation uses.",
